{
  "id": "2026.08.12-defst-share-fix",
  "created": "2026-08-12T22:43:52+00:00",
  "note": "Hold DEF/ST out of the offensive share denominator",
  "verdict": "KEPT_WITH_JUSTIFICATION",
  "justification": "Anytime TD xgb Top-1 50.8% -> 53.4% (+2.56pp, 3.6 se, p=0.000, 47 games won to 18 lost) with Brier also better (0.09121 -> 0.09019). Top-5 falls 94.8% -> 93.3% and AUC 0.8413 -> 0.8320. The Top-5 loss is the honest price of no longer covering defences by accident: the old path bought that coverage by publishing a 15%-likely defence as the game's most likely scorer in 131 of 1,131 games, at a mean probability of 0.908. AUC falls because the classifier's within-DEF/ST ranking is 0.54, barely better than chance, so restoring the honest number restores an honestly weak ordering; ranking defences properly is the follow-up. Top-1 is the objective and it is what improved.",
  "parent": "2026.08.12-baseline-remeasured",
